%I A399851 #16 Sep 20 2026 19:25:35
%S A399851 0,4,39,356,2889,21342,148193,970121,6032125,35849898,204645488,
%T A399851 1126462220,5999142412,30999375400,155798355411,763194756868,
%U A399851 3650648551166,17079277288591,78262894985345,351708873998430,1551843168592202,6729702902397750,28709867701366936
%N A399851 Number of tripartite (or 3-dimensional vector) partitions of (n, n, n) into distinct parts containing at least one mixed part.
%C A399851 A part (i, j, k) is mixed if it has at least two strictly positive coordinates. In contrast, a pure part lies on a single axis, having the form (i, 0, 0), (0, j, 0), or (0, 0, k).
%C A399851 This sequence counts the partitions of (n, n, n) into strictly distinct parts that contain at least one mixed part.
%C A399851 Partitions containing only pure parts decouple into three independent strictly distinct integer partitions of n, counted by A000009(n)^3. Subtracting these from the total number of strictly distinct tripartite partitions of (n, n, n) (which is A219560(n)) gives a(n).
%C A399851 Equivalently, the number of factorizations of p^n * q^n * r^n into strictly distinct factors > 1 containing at least one mixed factor (a factor divisible by at least two distinct primes from {p, q, r}), for any three distinct primes p, q, and r.
%C A399851 a(0) = 0 because the empty partition has no parts.
%C A399851 The 2-dimensional analog is A396961.
%D A399851 P. A. MacMahon, Combinatory Analysis, Cambridge Univ. Press, London and New York, Vol. 1, 1915 and Vol. 2, 1916.
%H A399851 Jishnu Babu Ranitha, <a href="/A399851/b399851.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..40</a>
%F A399851 a(n) = A219560(n) - A000009(n)^3.
%F A399851 a(n) = [x^n y^n z^n] G(x,y,z) - ([x^n] P(x))^3, where G(x,y,z) = Product_{i,j,k>=0, i+j+k>0} (1 + x^i * y^j * z^k) and P(x) = Product_{i>=1} (1 + x^i).
%e A399851 a(1) = 4: The total number of strictly distinct partitions of (1,1,1) is A219560(1) = 5. The only pure partition is {(1,0,0), (0,1,0), (0,0,1)}. The remaining 4 partitions ({(1,1,1)}, {(1,1,0), (0,0,1)}, {(1,0,1), (0,1,0)}, {(0,1,1), (1,0,0)}) contain at least one mixed part, so a(1) = 5 - 1^3 = 4.
%e A399851 a(2) = 39: The total number of distinct partitions of (2,2,2) is A219560(2) = 40. Exactly 1 partition contains only pure parts ({(2,0,0), (0,2,0), (0,0,2)} since A000009(2) = 1). The remaining 39 partitions contain at least one mixed part, so a(2) = 40 - 1^3 = 39.
%t A399851 max = 22; se = Series[Sum[(-1)^(m - 1)/m * (1/((1 - x^m)*(1 - y^m)*(1 - z^m)) - 1), {m, 1, max}], {x, 0, max}, {y, 0, max}, {z, 0, max}]; coes = CoefficientList[Exp[se], {x, y, z}]; Table[coes[[n + 1, n + 1, n + 1]] - PartitionsQ[n]^3, {n, 0, max}]
%o A399851 (Python)
%o A399851 def lista(n_max):
%o A399851     m = n_max + 1
%o A399851     dp = [[[0] * m for _ in range(m)] for _ in range(m)]
%o A399851     dp[0][0][0] = 1
%o A399851     for c1 in range(m):
%o A399851         for c2 in range(m):
%o A399851             for c3 in range(m):
%o A399851                 if c1 == 0 and c2 == 0 and c3 == 0: continue
%o A399851                 for i1 in range(m - 1, c1 - 1, -1):
%o A399851                     for i2 in range(m - 1, c2 - 1, -1):
%o A399851                         for i3 in range(m - 1, c3 - 1, -1):
%o A399851                             dp[i1][i2][i3] += dp[i1 - c1][i2 - c2][i3 - c3]
%o A399851     q = [1] + [0] * n_max
%o A399851     for i in range(1, m):
%o A399851         for x in range(n_max, i - 1, -1):
%o A399851             q[x] += q[x - i]
%o A399851     return [dp[n][n][n] - q[n]**3 for n in range(m)]
%o A399851 print(lista(22))
%Y A399851 Cf. A000009, A001055, A219560 (Column k=3 of A219585), A219585, A219678, A395808, A396961 (2-dimensional analog), A398607, A399611 (unrestricted totally mixed counterpart).
